  "summary": "Several studies have applied transformer models to customer churn prediction with varying results. Iyer et al. (2019) [D0084] used attention-only encoder architectures on the AgriSat dataset, reporting a MAPE of 0.675. Moreau et al. (2018) [D0082] also used attention-only encoder architectures but on the IEEE-CIS dataset, achieving an F1 score of 0.728. Tanaka et al. (2025) [D0083] employed self-attention sequence models on the GEFCom dataset, reporting a MAPE of 0.646. Zhou et al. (2020) [D0081] used self-attention sequence models on the ChurnBench dataset, achieving an AUROC of 0.679. Moreau et al. (2021) [D0085] used decentralised model updates on the HateCheck dataset, reporting a MAPE of 0.697.",
